# acc.add(x) of Accumulator<T, 1> (milestone2.md, "The accumulator"): the running sum s plus x, as
# add_1_1, and the running sum a of the magnitudes of what was added, plus |x| rounded to nearest. x
# is a value of the program: it passes through guard before both additions (rule R3); s and a are
# limbs of the accumulator. The count n is not a limb here: an integer of the header
# (std::size_t), exact where a count in T would round past 2^p, added on a merge, and converted
# to T only for bound_dot_k(n) and acc_radius_k, which require a count of T.
kernel:        acc_add_1
input:         stored s
input:         stored a
input:         x
output:        t
output:        b
value:         s+x
requires:      nonneg a
ensures:       rounded t nearest
ensures:       error t R c=1/(1+u) k=1 t=0
ensures:       rounded b nearest value=a+abs(x)
theorem:       proofs/theories/AccKernels.v acc_add_1_correct
ieee_spec_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeAccKernels.v acc_add_1_ieee_correct
min_precision: 1
source:        add_1_1 on a guarded element, and the sum of the magnitudes (milestone2.md)
license:       proof: MIT
status:        proved
ieee:          spec
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   b, the sum of magnitudes, does not reach t: its claim is read where b is finite (an entry about an output group other than the first), and where b is +inf the mask ok of acc_radius_k is false

g  = guard(x)
t  = add(s, g)
ag = abs(g)
b  = add(a, ag)
